  "decision_summary": "The current preferred family is PETSc SNES `newtonls` with backtracking line search and a non-LU Biot stack. `snes_default` remains the cleanest match to the public supported surface, while explicit `gmres + ilu` is the stable Biot family that survives both probes. Within that family, `ksp_gmres_restart=50` is currently the fastest passing fixed2 variant, but LU-backed Biot cases and all tested Newton fixed2 variants remain unsupported by the evidence.",
  "findings": [
    "SNES with a non-LU Biot stack remains the only family with passing fixed2 cases in this investigation.",
    "LU is the clearest cross-probe failure ingredient in the Biot stack.",
    "All tested Newton variants on fixed2 failed to advance, including higher max-iteration and damped variants.",
    "Fixed2 is stricter than Task 2: `snes_biot_preonly_ilu` passes on Task 2 but still fails on fixed2.",
    "The fastest passing fixed2 case in the current non-LU sweep is `snes_biot_gmres_ilu_restart50` at about 30.07 s total."
  ],
  "framing_paragraphs": [
    "This study exists because the public Lean surface is SNES-first, but some internal V&V lanes still relied on Newton or behaved differently when swapped to SNES. The practical question was whether that mismatch reflected a real nonlinear-solver difference or a smaller problem in backend activation, option plumbing, or linear-solver defaults.",
    "To isolate that, the investigation fixed the physics and changed one solver dimension at a time. `canonical_disk_fixed2` was used as the fast public coupled probe, while the Task 2 coupled strip lane was kept as the confirmation lane. The matrices on this page compare backend choice, Biot linear-stack choice, and monitored residual behavior so the conclusions are tied to reproducible evidence rather than one-off anecdotes."
  ],
